WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:00.911
Look up.

00:00:00.911 --> 00:00:01.622
Yes, me.

00:00:01.622 --> 00:00:04.873
I am Hope, and I have a story for you.

00:00:05.323 --> 00:00:07.513
Long ago I was a young blue whale.

00:00:07.513 --> 00:00:08.013
A girl.

00:00:08.013 --> 00:00:10.078
The ocean was my whole world.

00:00:10.528 --> 00:00:14.149
Then, on the morning of 25 March 1891,

00:00:14.149 --> 00:00:16.627
I stranded on a sandbar.

00:00:17.077 --> 00:00:19.388
It was the mouth of Wexford Harbour, in

00:00:19.388 --> 00:00:19.908
Ireland.

00:00:19.908 --> 00:00:21.948
Far from the deep water I knew.

00:00:22.398 --> 00:00:24.888
My skeleton, all four and a half

00:00:24.888 --> 00:00:27.907
tonnes, was sold to the Natural History

00:00:27.907 --> 00:00:28.511
Museum.

00:00:28.511 --> 00:00:29.893
For 250 pounds!

00:00:30.343 --> 00:00:33.113
From 1934, I hung in the Mammal Hall.

00:00:33.113 --> 00:00:36.133
Decades of quiet, watching from above.

00:00:36.582 --> 00:00:39.458
Then, July 2017: Hintze Hall.

00:00:39.458 --> 00:00:42.335
I took the place of Dippy the

00:00:42.335 --> 00:00:45.270
Diplodocus, here since 1979.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.565
I am 25.2 metres long.

00:00:47.565 --> 00:00:50.302
Big enough to carry a big name.

00:00:50.753 --> 00:00:52.671
They named me Hope: a symbol of

00:00:52.671 --> 00:00:55.069
humanity's power to shape a sustainable

00:00:55.069 --> 00:00:55.549
future.

00:00:55.549 --> 00:00:57.178
That part is up to you.
